Stress–life, strain–life and variable-amplitude damage (@mech-fatigue-models: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mechanical-engineering, #source "../sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY", #source "../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W", #mechanical-engineering "Crack-growth-life-and-inspection-information.lingua#r_5PQF88R4JPTQFQ0KEAV47WY7DW") { r_7QN3FJY3D4ZSB9643BEX9QYSXS
**Read:** [Modules in Mechanics of Materials — David Roylance](../sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY), Fatigue; [Applied Mechanics of Solids — Allan F. Bower](../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W), section 9.2 and its problems. Use the shared fatigue sources to inspect the original test basis rather than selecting a curve by alloy name alone.

Stress–life models describe a tested relation between cycle amplitude and life under stated conditions. Strain–life relations separate elastic and plastic strain contributions and can better represent cyclic plasticity. Mean-stress corrections, surface/size adjustments and notch factors are models whose calibration domain must be retained.

Palmgren–Miner accumulation writes D = Σ n_i/N_i using cycle counts n_i and constant-amplitude lives N_i. A chosen failure condition D ≈ 1 is empirical. It ignores sequence effects in its basic form; reversing the order of identical counted blocks leaves D unchanged even when a real crack or residual stress would evolve differently.

If one block has 10,000 cycles against a stated life of 100,000 and another has 2,000 against 20,000, the simple account gives D = 0.2. It does not establish exactly five such blocks to failure without validation of the model, data and history. Rainflow counting requires a declared signal, turning-point convention and treatment of incomplete cycles.

**Work:** Compare stress–life and strain–life accounts for a load history with local yielding. Independently count a small hand-drawn variable history before using software. Quantify sensitivity to mean stress, surface condition and material scatter, and identify a loading sequence that the simple linear accumulation cannot distinguish.

**Return:** [Mechanical engineering and machine design](../Mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design.lingua#r_0017YZ63HZBZ4P4WD8DECVWE4R).
